  {
    "slug": "ai-use",
    "title": "How I use AI",
    "sub": "",
    "style": "Page",
    "replace": true,
    "menu": "",
    "footer": "Site",
    "link": "",
    "linkPage": "",
    "words": "AI use",
    "hide": false,
    "body": "<p>This site was designed and coded with help from Claude, an AI model made by Anthropic. I directed the design, made the decisions, and reviewed every change. From here, I edit the HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and hosting setup myself.</p><h2 id=\"what-ai-helped-with\">What AI helped with</h2><ul><li>Layout and code</li><li>Research, and checking links and sources</li><li>The color analysis and chart in my moodboard essay</li><li>First drafts of some page copy, which I then rewrote or approved</li></ul><h2 id=\"what-ai-didnt-do\">What AI didn&#39;t do</h2><p>My notes and opinions are my own writing. My photographs are mine.</p><h2 id=\"labels\">Labels</h2><p>Anything drafted with AI carries an <span class=\"ai-pill\" title=\"Drafted with AI. See the AI use page.\">AI drafted</span> label, on the piece itself and wherever it&#39;s listed. That includes the example essays and the placeholder images, like the moodboard chart and the <a href=\"#\" data-page=\"bookmarks\" class=\"ab-link\">Shelf</a> covers. When I rewrite a piece myself, the label comes off.</p>",
    "order": 31
  },
